port Analyst\", \"company\": \"Tata Consultancy Services\", \"endDate\": \"Tue Dec 13\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Wed Sep 12\", \"description\": \"Client: HDFC Life Insurance | Nov 2018 – Jun 2020 Delivered production support for Communication Hub (CHUB) applications, investigating and resolving user-facing issues. • Developed SQL queries to retrieve, validate, and reconcile application data for client reporting. • Analyzed Java application logic to diagnose policy-related issues and pinpoint whether root causes originated in CRM or Communication Hub systems. • Developed Java enhancements for DOB, DEATH_TYPE, DATE_OF_DEATH, beneficiary information, and other client-driven requirements. • Developed and deployed application changes across production and non-production environments for batch and real-time processes. • Prepared communication reports to verify data consistency between CHUB and HDFC systems. • Investigated and resolved high-priority production incidents within defined SLAs. • Developed application tags, including DOB, CLIENT_TYPE, and DEPENDENCY, based on client requirements. • Earned the Beyond Performance Award (January 2020) for contributions to HDFC Life Insurance. Client: GSK Healthcare | Sep 2020 – Jun 2021 • Supported production operations and monitored scheduled jobs across application environments. • Executed front-end and back-end jobs and investigated failures using IPM. • Performed production support activities, including server-bounce validation and environment checks. • Used Unix commands to support application and server operations. • Analyzed MDM-related tables to identify failure and duplicate records. • Resolved high-priority incidents through ServiceNow and Remedy. Client: GSK RAMOS NG | Jun 2021 – Dec 2022 • Led issue identification, root-cause analysis, and production support for Clinical Trial Supply applications. • Supported development, testing, documentation, and implementation of application changes. • Performed monthly database requests, downtime activities, and patch activities across four environments. • Developed and implemented application changes based on evolving client requirements. • Investigated and resolved data-correction requests through controlled, validated data updates. • Developed application fixes and supported deployments across Development, UAT, and Production environments. • Participated in Agile/Scrum ceremonies to align support and development priorities. • Provided L2 support for GSK Clinical Trial Supply applications.\"}, {\"title\": \"Solution Engineer\", \"company\": \"LabVantage Solutions\", \"endDate\": \"Thu Jan 01\", \"isCurrent\": true, \"startDate\": \"Fri Dec 30\", \"description\": \"• Develop and customize LabVantage LIMS applications to meet client-specific laboratory requirements across multiple active projects. • Configure and maintain Master Data, Departmental Security, Event Plans, SDC Rules, Property Details, and Maint/List/View pages to keep LIMS instances aligned with evolving client specifications. • Build Java-based custom actions for material creation, batch creation and modification, cancellation handling, and preliminary disposition updates, reducing manual processing effort. • Design and modify Event Plans, Action Blocks, and Groovy-based workflows to automate stability pull reminders, sample status updates, and external system status synchronization. • Configure end-to-end sample workflows, including conditions, visits, timepoints, plans, and work-order lifecycles, to support laboratory operations. • Configure Environmental Monitoring schedules, locations, and sample points to support regulatory monitoring requirements. • Implement custom Action Codes, SDC Rules, and SQL queries to satisfy functional and technical specifications. • Configure Advanced Toolbars, buttons, tramlines, and tramstops across List, View, and Maintenance pages to improve usability. • Build and validate application changes through Ant-based build processes and perform installer validation prior to release. • Develop and debug Java code using IntelliJ IDEA to support ongoing customization work. • Design and maintain BarTender label templates for samples, products, consumables, and Environmental Monitoring workflows. • Support JasperReports through report structure analysis and targeted report customization. • Investigate application and integration issues through LabVantage log analysis, resolving defects efficiently. • Collaborate with clients and internal teams using Agile methodology, JIRA, and Confluence to manage delivery. • Contributed to CIBA ALCON VISION, MITHRA, INSELS, and BAYER_WUPPERTAL client projects.\"}]','[{\"year\": \"2018\", \"degree\": \"Electronics and Communication Engineering\", \"result\": \"73%\", \"institution\": \"Sree Vidyanikethan Engineering College\"}]','[]','[]','[]','[]',NULL,NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"/uploads/resumes/pattan-mohammed-sayeed-khan-1790577182-213.pdf\", \"title\": \"PATTAN MOHAMMED SAYEED KHAN\", \"isDefault\": false}, {\"url\": \"/uploads/resumes/pattan-mohammed-sayeed-khan-1790577185-116.pdf\", \"title\": \"PATTAN MOHAMMED SAYEED KHAN\", \"isDefault\": false}]','[]'),('0128a4ec-8f86-4aec-909f-b5ba877b648c','96931234-9492-4b4e-876f-84cc92010891','Azure cloud Support Escalation Engineer',NULL,'Azure cloud Support Escalation Engineer',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"AWS\", \"Git\", \"Jenkins\", \"JIRA\", \"Linux\", \"DevOps\", \"Ansible\", \"Ansible\", \"Kubernetes\", \"Jenkins\", \"DevOps\", \"Grafana\", \"Helm\", \"Git\", \"Cloud Infrastructure\", \"Cloud Computing\", \"Ansible\", \"Linux\", \"Nagios\", \"OpenStack\", \"OpenShift\", \"OpenShift\", \"OpenStack\", \"Splunk\", \"Prometheus\", \"TerraForm\", \"OpenShift\", \"UNIX\"]','PUBLIC','2025-05-16 11:31:59.000000','2026-10-21 07:09:04.000000','[{\"title\": \"Azure cloud Support Escalation Engineer\", \"company\": \"Microsoft Corp\", \"endDate\": \"\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"\", \"description\": \"\"}]','[]','[]','[