ion support. Experienced in \r\nbuilding and leading cross-functional teams, defining platform roadmaps, \r\nand translating complex technical challenges into scalable business \r\nsolutions.','Manager – Digital Twin & Asset Modelling',6,NULL,'/uploads/resumes/cv-1787667972-750.pdf',NULL,'[\"Digital Transformation\", \"AI/ML\", \"Cloud Computing\", \"Linux\", \"JIRA\", \"Confluence\", \"Microservices\", \"Kubernetes\", \"AWS\", \"Azure\", \"Agile\", \"IIoT\", \"MS Office\", \"Scrum Framework\", \"SCADA\", \"MQTT\", \"PLC\", \"Generative AI\"]','PUBLIC','2026-08-26 01:55:18.000000','2026-10-21 07:09:05.000000','[{\"title\": \"Manager – Digital Twin & Asset Modelling\", \"company\": \"Siemens Energy India Ltd\", \"endDate\": \"Thu Aug 20\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Fri Sep 10\", \"description\": \"• Drive Digital Twin roadmap from physics models to cloud \\r\\ndeployment. \\r\\n• Build high-performing teams across simulation, IoT, and testing. \\r\\n• Own end-to-end Digital Twin platform delivery across architecture, \\r\\nphysics modeling, IIoT integration, and customer commissioning. \\r\\n• Bridge OT–IT by integrating sensor data with simulations outputs. \\r\\n• Lead cross-functional engineers (modeling, IoT, testing, platform) \\r\\nto deliver real-time, decision-grade digital twins. \\r\\n• Establish test cases to ensure model accuracy and operational trust. \\r\\n• Defined Digital Twin lifecycle frameworks including calibration, \\r\\nFAT/SAT, deployment, and operational handover. \\r\\n• Led India’s first cloud-based Digital Twin commissioning, enabling \\r\\npredictive maintenance and performance optimization. \\r\\n• Influence platform evolution through structured customer feedback \\r\\n• Drive asset intelligence use cases: anomaly detection, what-if \\r\\nsimulation, performance benchmarking, and operational insights. \\r\\n• Partner with product, platform, and customer stakeholders to \\r\\ntranslate business needs into scalable technical solutions. \\r\\n• Mentor engineers and drive digital twin adoption through training \\r\\nworkshops with management, engineering teams, and customers. \\r\\n• Used Reduced Order Models (ROMs) integrated with test data, \\r\\nenabling near real-time performance prediction.\"}, {\"title\": \"Senior CFD Engineer\", \"company\": \"ASM Technologies Ltd\", \"endDate\": \"Tue Aug 10\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Wed Jul 10\", \"description\": \"• Performed unsteady CFD simulations to optimize gas flow, \\r\\npressure, and velocity in process chambers. \\r\\n• Delivered CFD-based thermal analysis for CVD processes, \\r\\nenabling precise temperature and deposition control. \\r\\n• Validated 3D CFD models against test data & accelerating design.\"}, {\"title\": \"Senior CFD Engineer\", \"company\": \"MAN Energy Solutions\", \"endDate\": \"Sat Jul 20\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Sat Jan 10\", \"description\": \"• Standardized CFD simulation workflow for intake and exhaust \\r\\nports to evaluate air flow distribution and flow coefficient. \\r\\n• Redefined 3D CFD methodology for I.C. engine cooling, which \\r\\nreduced computational time by ~70%. \\r\\n• Performed 3D CFD simulations of fuel injector nozzles to study \\r\\nspray, flow dynamics, and cavitation. \\r\\n• Collaborated with design, testing & engineering teams to improve \\r\\nnozzle geometry, increasing discharge coefficient. \\r\\n• Performed CFD studies on CAC casing to improve diffuser \\r\\nefficiency, pressure drop, and velocity uniformity.\"}]','[{\"year\": \"2012\", \"degree\": \"Master of Technology\", \"result\": \"68\", \"institution\": \"Visvesvaraya National Institute of Technology\"}]','[]','[]','[]','[]',NULL,NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"/uploads/resumes/cv-1787667972-750.pdf\", \"title\": \"CV\", \"isDefault\": false}]','[]'),('0d3e3d71-bc60-45a5-b53a-a9dc94394a21','c27ff930-f6b7-4b92-b369-4dc3e5d3035f','Test Resume179','Test Resume179','Software Deve',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\".NET\"]'