roughput and system reliability across the \\r\\nglobal estate. \\r\\n• Built POS terminal screens in WPF and XAML using the MVVM pattern — data binding, commands, reusable user \\r\\ncontrols and shared styles — for touch-screen operation on in-store hardware. \\r\\n• Developed ASP.NET Core Web API services for remote order handling, receiving orders placed outside the store and \\r\\nmaking them available to the WPF POS application, which notified staff for in-store fulfillment. \\r\\n• Implemented add and remove item operations on remotely placed orders, keeping the POS terminal’s order state \\r\\nconsistent with changes made through the remote channel. \\r\\n• Developed core POS features including MVP Rewards enrolment and redemption via card swipe, phone lookup and \\r\\nQR scan, using C# and .NET Framework. \\r\\n• Delivered fiscal device compliance for the German market, ensuring accurate sales recording and audit readiness \\r\\nunder local regulatory requirements. \\r\\n• Built and integrated back-office modules with Entity Framework and SQL Server, extending reporting and \\r\\nadministrative capability. \\r\\n• Resolved complex production incidents within defined SLA response times, working with L3 support and cross\\r\\nfunctional teams to minimize downtime across globally distributed store systems. \\r\\n• Implemented polyglot persistence by using different data stores for different workload requirements, including \\r\\nrelational databases for transactional data and NoSQL databases for high-volume, flexible, or low-latency \\r\\nworkloads. \\r\\n• Authored root-cause documentation and defect reports that shortened diagnosis time for recurring production issues \\r\\nand became reference material for the support team.\"}, {\"title\": \"Senior Software Engineer\", \"company\": \"Struengineer\", \"endDate\": \"Wed Apr 14\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Wed Nov 20\", \"description\": \"This is a Web-based application for a structural design purpose. I worked on UI as well as back-end of this application. This \\r\\napplication focuses on the precast tools. \\r\\n• Designed and delivered Restful APIs in .NET Core using ASP.NET Core Web API, supporting advisor oversight, \\r\\nsupervisory review workflows and regulatory reporting across the compliance platform. \\r\\n• Built a generic user preference service in .NET Core, giving all modules a single reusable, configuration-driven way to \\r\\nstore and retrieve per-user settings instead of separate implementations per feature. \\r\\n• Built the .NET Core API that keeps the on-premise legacy application in sync with the new AWS-hosted platform — \\r\\ningesting advisor submissions landed nightly from SQL DB and distributing each document across multiple related \\r\\nSQL Server tables, so compliance records stay reconciled across both systems of record during parallel running. \\r\\n• Owned the document-to-relational mapping for this flow, translating nested submission documents into the legacy \\r\\nnormalized schema so downstream legacy processes required no modification. \\r\\n• Worked across the full stack on the compliance platform — .NET Core APIs on the backend and Angular 15 on the \\r\\nfront end — coordinating contract changes across both layers. \\r\\n• Optimised API payloads by restructuring request/response serialization to exclude null fields, reducing payload size \\r\\nand improving response times. \\r\\n• Built and deployed serverless .NET Core services on AWS (Lambda, API Gateway) with CloudWatch instrumentation \\r\\nfor monitoring, alerting and production diagnostics. \\r\\n• Managed CI/CD pipelines in Octopus Deploy and owned release and deployment activities through to production. \\r\\n• Acted as the point of contact for the legacy integration — coordinating schema mapping with the legacy application \\r\\nteam, investigating synchronization discrepancies in production, and advising on cut-over behavior..\"}, {\"title\": \"Software Developer\", \"company\": \"Winner Software Pvt. Ltd.\", \"endDate\": \"Sun Nov 10\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Mon Sep 11\", \"description\": \" Project Description: \\r\\nDesktop-based examination application designed for subjective/typing-based exams, supporting the complete \\r\\nexamination workflow from data and file processing through marking, reporting and result generation. Worked across \\r\\nboth UI and backend, contributing to end-to-end application development and maintenance. \\r\\n• Technologies: C#.NET, WPF, Telerik UI, ADO.NET, WinForms, Crystal Reports \\r\\nFramework: .NET Framework 4 \\r\\nIDE: Visual Studio 2010 \\r\\n• Developed end-to-end application functionality in C#.NET and WPF, implementing both UI workflows and backend \\r\\nprocessing for the examination platform. \\r\\n• Implemented database operations using ADO.NET, leveraging Data Adapter, Data Reader and DataSet for efficient \\r\\nreading, updating and processing of examination data. \\r\\n• Developed Hall Ticket generation functionality using WinForms and Crystal Reports, enabling formatted, printable \\r\\nexamination documents. \\r\\n• Contributed to functional and unit testing, identifying defects, validating business workflows and ensuring \\r\\napplication functionality met requirements. \\r\\n• Provided maintenance and enhancement support for existing code, troubleshooting issues and implementing \\r\\nchanges across the application. \\r\\n• Worked closely with the core development team throughout the product lifecycle, supporting feature development, \\r\\nintegration and delivery activities. \\r\\n• Supervised junior developers throughout the migration project lifecycle, providing technical guidance, reviewing \\r\\nimplementation and helping resolve development issues.\"}]','[{\"year\": \"2017\", \"degree\": \"MBA, Computer Science\", \"result\": \"63\", \"institution\": \"Yashwantrao Chavan Maharashtra University\"}]','[]','[]','[]','[]',NULL,NULL,'[]','[{\"ur