amic SQL.\\r\\n Automated critical batch operations (e.g., usage uploads, nightly reconciliations, service status updates) using \\r\\nUNIX shell scripts\\r\\n integrated with PL/SQL, ensuring reliable job execution via `cron`\"}, {\"title\": \"Technical Lead\", \"company\": \"Atos SynteL\", \"endDate\": \"Mon May 30\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Sat Jul 10\", \"description\": \"Designed and developed Oracle SQL/PLSQL-based solutions for end-to-end \\r\\nstudent loan management systems, including modules\\r\\n for loan origination, disbursement, repayment schedules, and delinquency tracking.\\r\\n Created and maintained PL/SQL packages, procedures, and triggers to manage large volumes of student loan applications,\\r\\n repayment transactions, and interest accruals, ensuring accuracy and compliance with lending rules.\\r\\n Engineered high-performance data models and implemented \\r\\npartitioning, \\r\\nmaterialized views, and \\r\\nindexing strategies to optimize\\r\\n performance for financial reporting, borrower statements, and regulatory submissions.\\r\\n Automated batch processes for loan disbursements, daily interest calculations, and repayment postings using \\r\\nUNIX shell scripting\\r\\n integrated with PL/SQL and scheduled via `cron`.\\r\\n Collaborated with product owners, loan servicing teams, and QA analysts to capture business requirements and translate them\\r\\n into scalable, maintainable database components.\\r\\n Conducted code reviews and implemented PL/SQL tuning techniques (bulk collect, forall, optimizer hints) to ensure efficient\\r\\n handling of student loan portfolios across academic cycles.\"}, {\"title\": \"Senior Software Enginee\", \"company\": \"IVL Pvt. Ltd.\", \"endDate\": \"Tue Jul 20\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Mon Sep 10\", \"description\": \"Led the design, development, and optimization of complex PL/SQL programs, procedures, functions, and packages to implement\\r\\n core business logic for large-scale enterprise systems.\\r\\n Architected scalable, high-performance database solutions to support transactional, analytical, and batch processing workloads in\\r\\n Oracle environments (10g/11g/12c/19c).\\r\\n Wrote high-complexity SQL queries involving subqueries, analytical functions, dynamic SQL, pivot/unpivot logic, and\\r\\n performance-critical joins.\\r\\n Conducted code optimization and performance tuning using Explain Plan, SQL Trace, DBMS_PROFILER, AWR reports, and Oracle\\r\\n Hints to minimize I/O and response time.\\r\\n Designed and implemented exception handling, logging, and instrumentation frameworks for PL/SQL components to ensure\\r\\n production-level reliability.\\r\\n Reviewed functional and technical requirements, collaborated with business analysts, and translated them into modular, reusable\\r\\n database components.\\r\\n Authored High-Level Design (HLD) and Low-Level Design (LLD) documents, covering architecture, logic flow, exception strategy,\\r\\n and data dependencies.\\r\\n Managed code versioning, deployments, and peer code reviews to maintain quality and compliance in agile and DevOps\\r\\n environments.\\r\\n Provided technical leadership to developers by setting coding standards, assigning tasks, and reviewing complex SQL and PL/SQL\\r\\n implementations.\\r\\n Collaborated with front-end and integration teams to support seamless data access, performance optimization, and debugging of\\r\\n system-wide issues.\\r\\n Handled production issues, root cause analysis, and defect resolution for performance bottlenecks, data mismatches, and long\\r\\nrunning jobs.\\r\\n Led schema design, normalization, indexing, partitioning, and stored object management for new modules and large-scale data\\r\\n migrations\"}, {\"title\": \"Software Engineer\", \"company\": \"Sourceedge Software Technologies Pvt. Ltd\", \"endDate\": \"Mon Jul 30\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Sun Dec 10\", \"description\": \"Design, develop, and optimize co