glot persistence (PostgreSQL + MongoDB + Redis).','Java Developer',4,NULL,'/uploads/resumes/cv-1779794698-896.pdf',NULL,'[\"Java\", \"J2EE\", \"JPA (Java Persistence Api)\", \"Hibernate\", \"AWS\", \"JWT (Json Web Tokens)\", \"Gradle\", \"Grafana\", \"SQL\", \"PL/SQL\", \"Spring Boot\", \"Spring Boot\", \"SNS (Simple Notification Service)\", \"Swagger\", \"SNS (Simple Notification Service)\", \"Mockito\"]','PUBLIC','2026-05-26 22:50:45.000000','2026-10-21 07:09:05.000000','[{\"title\": \"Java Developer\", \"company\": \"Encora Technology\", \"endDate\": \"Wed May 20\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Thu May 15\", \"description\": \"• Architected and developed cloud-native microservices using Java 21 and Spring Boot 3.x deployed on AWS \\r\\nEKS with Kubernetes for auto-scaling and zero-downtime deployments. \\r\\n• Engineered Java 21 Virtual Threads (Project Loom) to improve concurrent request throughput by 30% on high\\r\\ntraffic RESTful Web Services handling 500K+ daily requests. \\r\\n• Designed and maintained high-performance RESTful APIs and event-driven data pipelines using Apache \\r\\nKafka, processing 500K+ messages per day with sub-second latency. \\r\\n• Secured 10+ microservice endpoints with Spring Security (JWT + OAuth 2.0 RBAC), eliminating unauthorized \\r\\naccess incidents across 500K daily requests across 3 environments. \\r\\n• Optimized PostgreSQL average query time by 40% through composite indexing, rewriting N+1 ORM queries, \\r\\nand tuning HikariCP connection pool settings. \\r\\n• Integrated Elasticsearch for full-text metadata search, reducing search API response time from 800ms to \\r\\nunder 80ms, enabling real-time search across 2M+ metadata records. \\r\\n• Redesigned Jenkins CI/CD pipeline with Docker and GitHub Actions, cutting deployment time from 2 hours to \\r\\n35 minutes — a 70% reduction in release cycle time. \\r\\n• Implemented distributed tracing with Spring Cloud Sleuth, Zipkin, and Prometheus/Grafana dashboards for \\r\\nend-to-end observability across 10+ microservices. \\r\\n• Mentored 2 junior developers on Spring Boot Microservices, TDD, and code review best practices, improving \\r\\nteam delivery velocity by 20%\"}, {\"title\": \"Java Backend Developer\", \"company\": \"Infosys Limited\", \"endDate\": \"Thu Jun 20\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Tue Jul 05\", \"description\": \"• Developed and maintained 6+ backend modules for US-based insurance and analytics clients using Java 8, \\r\\nSpring Boot, Spring MVC, Hibernate ORM, and Spring Data JPA. \\r\\n• Designed RESTful and SOAP web services integrated with third-party insurance platforms, reducing data \\r\\nexchange errors by 25% across 10K+ daily policy transactions. \\r\\n• Implemented layered architecture (Controller, Service, DAO) following SOLID principles and Factory, Builder, \\r\\nand Singleton design patterns. \\r\\n• Deployed Java microservices on AWS Cloud (EC2, RDS) with Docker containers; configured Kubernetes \\r\\npods, services, and deployments for 99.9% availability. \\r\\n• Tuned Hibernate JPA mappings with lazy loading, fetch strategies, and second-level caching, improving data\\r\\nfetch latency by 30% on high-volume tables. \\r\\n• Maintained 85%+ code coverage with JUnit 5 and Mockito; integrated with Jenkins CI/CD to automatically \\r\\nblock failing builds from merging. \\r\\n• Followed GitFlow branching strategy using GitHub and Bitbucket for source control, code reviews, and \\r\\nproduction incident root-cause analysis. \\r\\n• Participated in full Agile Scrum lifecycle across 8+ sprints including sprint planning, backlog grooming, daily \\r\\nstand-ups, and retrospectives. \\r\\n• Used Log4j, SLF4J, and ELK Stack for structured logging; identified and resolved performance bottlenecks via \\r\\nthread dump analysis in production.\"}]','[{\"year\": \"2022\", \"degree\": \"Bachelor of Technology in Computer Science\", \"result\": \"75\", \"institution\": \"SASTRA Deemed University\