, collaborating with developers and QA teams in an\\r\\nAgile Scrum environment.\"}, {\"title\": \"QA Automation Test Engineer\", \"company\": \"Zopa Banll\", \"endDate\": \"Fri Jan 20\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Mon Jul 05\", \"description\": \"Analyzed business requirements, user stories, and functional specifications to understand application\\r\\nfunctionality and testing scope.\\r\\nPrepared detailed Test Scenarios, Test Cases, and Test Data based on business requirements and\\r\\nacceptance criteria.\\r\\nExecuted Smoke, Sanity, Functional, Regression, Integration, and User Acceptance Testing (UAT) to\\r\\nvalidate application quality.\\r\\nPerformed Positive, Negative, Boundary Value, Equivalence Partitioning, and Validation testing to ensure\\r\\ncomplete test coverage.\\r\\nConducted GUI, Cross-Browser, and Compatibility Testing to verify consistent application behavior\\r\\nacross supported browsers.\\r\\nIdentified, logged, tracked, and retested defects using JIRA, ensuring timely resolution and proper defect\\r\\nlifecycle management.\\r\\nVerified bug fixes through Regression Testing and collaborated closely with developers to resolve issues.\\r\\nPrepared Test Execution Reports, maintained testing documentation, and reported daily testing progress\\r\\nto stakeholders.\\r\\nParticipated in requirement review meetings, sprint planning, daily stand-ups, sprint reviews, and\\r\\nretrospectives in an Agile Scrum environment.\\r\\nWorked closely with Business Analysts, Developers, and QA team members to clarify requirements and\\r\\nensure high-quality software delivery\"}]','[{\"year\": \"2020\", \"degree\": \"BCOM(Computer Application)\", \"result\": \"63\", \"institution\": \"Cauvery College for Women\"}]','[]','[]','[]','[]',NULL,NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"/uploads/resumes/cv-1786119243-43.pdf\", \"title\": \"CV\", \"isDefault\": false}]','[]'),('6b38c985-ae15-46e0-ad34-b41cf5dd6c08','266b9908-3266-42bc-9000-14eb43cfb86a','Node.Js Developer',