iness Consulting\", \"company\": \"HSBC\", \"endDate\": \"Wed Apr 15\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Tue Jul 15\", \"description\": \"• Part of HSBC’s internal consulting team within the Group Strategy and Consulting function reporting directly to HSBC’s Group CEO. Role focuses on HSBC’s strategic and \\r\\nmarket direction agenda focusing market entry and market growth, identifying market efficiencies and restructuring needs, areas of cost optimization, operating model \\r\\ntransformation and proposition development \\r\\n• Enabling \\\"Future-Ready\\\" business models for the Group CEO’s Strategy function to navigate global economic reinvention \\r\\nKey Projects  \\r\\n• MENAT Network Markets Operating model design – Global Bank’s entity based in Dubai, United Arab Emirates  \\r\\nDefined the optimal operating model for the MENAT market branches – balancing front and back-office efficiency, CTB / RTB Cost Optimization, regulatory compliance \\r\\nand client delivery with a right-sized hub and spoke activity model \\r\\nEvaluated cost optimization opportunities across front. Middle and back-office functions leveraging “Hub and spoke” capabilities resulting in a cost reduction of 20% \\r\\n(AED 15M) across MENAT branches  \\r\\n• Country Network Banking Archetype creation and Target Operating Model design – Global Bank based in the UK, London, United Kingdom  \\r\\nLed the creation of the As-Is CIB (Commercial and International banking) market footprint and landscape (“Fact base”)  \\r\\nDefined a market archetype value framework to categorize 50+ markets capturing both qualitative and quantitative value aspects and levers for measures of success \\r\\nIdentified AED 50M in efficiency gains through the deployment of \\\"Market-in-a-Box\\\" digital operating models\"}, {\"title\": \"Management Consulting Manager\", \"company\": \"Accenture\", \"endDate\": \"Thu Jul 10\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Sun Oct 10\", \"description\": \"• Delivered consulting engagements across 4 countries, including UAE, focusing on digital strategy and customer experience design, use-cases design, operating model \\r\\ndesign, process re-engineering, and business transformation. Conducted due diligence studies, competitive benchmarking, and financial proposal development  \\r\\n• Led consulting business development by contributing to 15 consulting RFPs with a 40% conversion rate, generating new business bookings of approximately 8M AED. \\r\\n• Subject matter architect for 20 knowledge assets for internal portals, including pitch decks and offerings on digital financial services, banking post-merger integration \\r\\nand AI in payments. \\r\\nKey Projects \\r\\n• Corporate Banking modernization roadmap – Regional bank in South-East Asia \\r\\nLed the corporate banking modernization and initiatives revamp roadmap for the bank. Identified key gaps across customer experience, distribution strategy and product \\r\\ncapabilities and prioritized modernization initiatives. The strategy engagement resulted in securing a multi-year system implementation contract worth 6M AED. \\r\\n• Wholesale business fee income growth strategy – Regional bank in the UAE \\r\\nDeveloped a strategic roadmap to assess the decline in a bank’s income by analyzing market trends, competitive threats, and regulatory shifts. Recommended a phased \\r\\napproach, including quick wins, near-term initiatives, and long-term strategies such as competitive pricing, ESG-aligned offerings, and partnerships to drive growth. \\r\\nDesigned a roadmap to pivot from interest-margin reliance to fee-based growth. Projected a 12% increase in non-interest income by 2027 through the launch of ESG\\r\\naligned trade finance and BaaS platforms.  \\r\\n• Program Health check and Program Strategy – Large global bank in the United States of America \\r\\nDirected the migration strategy for the Payments modernization initiative for the world’s largest cross-border payment provider, covering 30%\"}, {\"title\": \"Consulting Manager\", \"company\": \"PwC\", \"endDate\": \"Sat Oct 30\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Sat Jun 10\", \"description\": \"• Led 8+ strategy engagements in digital payments, banking, and the public sector, covering transformation strategy and roadmaps, Mission and vision, operating models, \\r\\nand CX design. \\r\\n• Led and delivered 15 strategy consulting engagements over 4.5 years, with project profitability margins exceeding 35%. Consulting engagements spanned across 7 \\r\\ncountries, including the Middle East. \\r\\n• Led consulting business development efforts by contributing to nearly 30 business and strategy consulting RFPs, achieving a 30% conversion rate and generating nearly \\r\\n8M AED in new business.  \\r\\nKey Projects \\r\\n• Regulatory (VAT) and Digital Impact Assessment – Multinational Investment Bank, Dubai, United Arab Emirates \\r\\nConducted regulatory and digital impact assessment across bank’s business due to the newly introduced VAT regulation. Conceptualized business requirements and \\r\\ncreated build vs buy assessment framework. Delivered AED 25M efficiency gains via VAT compliance redesign across UAE and KSA business units.  \\r\\n• Regulatory (VAT) and Digital Impact Assessment – Mubadala, Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates \\r\\nLed a portfolio-wide regulatory impact assessment for 40+ legal entities. Mitigated >AED 50M in potential fines by designing a centralized governance framework and \\r\\nZATCA-compliant e-invoicing workflow. \\r\\n• Business and Process Redesign & Business Case Development – Government Housing Society, Caribbean region \\r\\nOptimized the housing society’s retail lending processes and developed a business case and prioritization framework to select implementation vendors for automating \\r\\nthe mortgage process, leading to nearly 20M AED reduction in Total cost of ownership through automated workflows and operational efficiencies. This led to an increase \\r\\nin Customer satisfaction and engagement by 10% 6 months post implementation. \\r\\n• Digital financial services Market Maturity Assessment & Interoperability Roadmap – Central Bank of West African States, Dakar, Senegal \\r\\nSuccessfully led creation of a data driven digital financial services market maturity assessment report and interoperability roadmap, impacting 147.5M people across 8 \\r\\nWAEMU countries through financial services interoperability. \\r\\n• Digital Payments Diagnostic & National Roadmap – UNCDF and Government of Bangladesh, Dhaka, Bangladesh \\r\\nLed development of the digital payments diagnostic and roadmap across key economic sector, with exhaustive data-analytics driven findings and roadmap launched by \\r\\nthe federal government and published on UNCDF website, guiding national digital payments adoption. Digital financial services Interventions and solutions proposed in \\r\\nthe roadmap laid the potential to transform key sectors impacting 37% of the country’s GDP and impacting 150 million people\"}]','[{\"year\": \"2015\", \"degree\": \"Master of Business Administration (MBA Finance)\", \"result\": \"68\", \"institution\": \"IMT Ghaziabad\"}]','[]','[]','[]','[]',NULL,NULL,'[]','[{\"url\": \"/uploads/resumes/cv-1776354026-933.pdf\", \"title\": \"CV\", \"isDefault\": false}]','[]'),('9199b9dc-f7fb-47ba-9de0-e8f93ad973c3','ddb0e32c-7a9a-482c-b8a7-9c689aeaeae6','Test Resume313','Test Resume313','Software Deve',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"Guidewire Automation Testing\"]','PUBLIC','2025-05-24 21:19:45.000000','2026-10-21 07:09:04.000000','[{\"title\": \"Software Deve\", \"company\": \"TCS\", \"endDate\": \"\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"\", \"description\": \"\"}]','[{\"year\": \"\", \"degree\": \"B.Tech\", \"result\": \"\", \"institution\": \"\"}]','[]','[]','[]','[]',NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]'),('919be874-975f-41e7-9227-09e0325f9817','b53dbab4-8f40-404c-9be3-133e84b44e50','Test Resume331','Test Resume331','Software Deve',2,NULL,NUL