R. Certified in ITIL Foundation in IT Service Management and Google Certified Data Analyst with expertise in data interpretation, contributing to organizational success.','ERP Senior SPECIALIST',6,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"Historian\", \"Mes\", \"SQL Server\", \"MYSQL\", \"SSMS\", \"AVEVA MES\", \"Siemens Opcenter\", \"Opcenter APS\", \"SAP\", \"Power BI\", \"SolarWinds\", \"Quality System Testing\", \"Visual Regression Testing\", \"Validation\"]','PUBLIC','2025-12-15 21:11:47.000000','2026-10-21 07:09:05.000000','[{\"title\": \"ERP Senior SPECIALIST\", \"company\": \"NTT Data\", \"endDate\": \"Sun Nov 30\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Sat Apr 05\", \"description\": \"•\\tDevelop and execute detailed test plans, test cases, and automation/manual scripts to validate system functionalities, process controls, and MES/ERP integrations across the EV battery lifecycle.\\r\\n•\\tPerform end-to-end testing of EV battery manufacturing processes (cell assembly, module/pack integration, charging/discharging cycles, BMS functionality) to ensure compliance with quality and safety standards\\r\\n•\\tIdentify, log, and track defects/issues in manufacturing or system workflows; collaborate with engineering and production teams for timely resolution.\\r\\n•\\tPrepare comprehensive test reports, including test execution results, defect logs, and traceability matrices, to provide visibility of quality status and compliance.\\r\\n•\\tProficient in building and managing factory models, workflows, transactions, user roles, container management, and portal customization using Opcenter Execution Core\\r\\n•\\tProficient in Siemens Opcenter EX Electronics with hands-on experience in modeling and executing electronics manufacturing processes, including SMT/THT assembly, panel registration, carrier and recipe management, real-time defect handling, Numbering ruling and integration of NPI Jobs.\\r\\n•\\tSkilled in configuring and operating Opcenter Intra Plant Logistics (IPL) for optimizing material flow between work centers; experienced in material pull/push logistics, container tracking, and line-side material delivery.\\r\\n•\\tTrained in Research, Development & Laboratory (RD&L) suite including Laboratory Management, Formula Workbench, and Specification Management\\r\\n•\\tGained hands-on knowledge of Siemens Opcenter APS, including planning vs scheduling concepts, data setup, rule configuration, material control, calendars, Gantt charts, and standard reporting features\"}, {\"title\": \"Senior Software Engineer\", \"company\": \"HCL Tech\", \"endDate\": \"Mon Mar 31\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Thu Feb 01\", \"description\": \"•\\tExperienced with AVEVA Products such as Thin Client, Object Console Management Console, and   MES’S client.\\r\\n•\\tIn depth knowledge on MES Modules like Quality, Performance and Operations.\\r\\n•\\tHands-on experience in Work Orders, Routes, BOM, Spec Management, Characteristics, Alarms. \\r\\n•\\tUtilized SAP COR1 and COR2 interfaces for efficient production order creation and modification.\\r\\n•\\tSuccessfully activated and validated MES licenses using the AVEVA System platform management console, including feature level verification and post deployment Validation.\\r\\n•\\tResponsible for maintaining food Production Plants, proactively identifying and addressing issues to ensure continuous and efficient operations.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n•\\tUtilized Stone branch for job Scheduling, proactively monitoring job executions and promptly escalating any job failures to clients and trying in identifying and deleting unnecessary jobs, optimizing system performance and resource utilization.\\r\\n•\\tProvided support for Cornerstone and Nice Label customer applications, ensuring seamless functionality and performance. Conducted functional and non-functional testing for new features, along with regression testing to validate system stability and prevent defects in existing functionalities.\\r\\n•\\tPerformed smoke testing before OS patching and firewall upgrades to validate system stability and core functionality. Conducted sanity testing post-upgrade to ensure that critical MES applications and production systems were operational, verifying successful implementation without impacting existing functionalities.\\r\\n•\\tIdentifying the priority of the incident based on the criticality & business impact and declaring it accordingly.\\r\\n•\\tCo-ordinating with CAB if any emergency change request required to resolve the incident.\\r\\n•\\tProvide timely & effective IT communication update about incidents to the users & internal stakeholders within the agreed SLA\\r\\n•\\tConfigured alerts in SolarWinds for 72 Windows servers across 8 manufacturing plants, tested alert generation based on different scenarios, and ensured continuous production uptime.\\r\\n•\\tConducted training for six new graduates on AVEVA MES domain knowledge and common client-reported issues, enhancing team expertise and readiness.\\r\\n•\\tUtilized Service Now for incident management, with strong knowledge in incident, change and problem management, including ticket creation and resolution.\\r\\n•\\tInteracted directly with clients to address and resolve security vulnerabilities, ensuring robust \\r\\nprotection and compliance.\"}, {\"title\": \"Analyst II Software Engineer\", \"company\": \"DXC Technology\", \"endDate\": \"Sat Feb 10\", \"isCurrent\": false, \"startDate\": \"Tue Aug 10\", \"description\": \"•\\tResponsible for maintaining servers at multiple manufacturing plants, involving the proactive monitoring of server health, performance metrics, and resource utilization to identify and address potential issues.\\r\\n•\\tGood Exposure to Wonder ware system Platform, wonder ware MES and Wonder ware Historian and Responsibilities involve resolving issues and providing support for HMI applications within the Wonder ware environment for food processing lines.\\r\\n•\\tPerformed offline license activation for AVEVA Manufacturing Execution System, ensuring secure and compliant deployment.\\r\\n•\\tPlayed a critical role in disaster recovery management by ensuring all MES systems and client applications were fully operational post-recovery. Conducted comprehensive testing, including disaster recovery validation, functional testing, performance testing, data integrity checks, connectivity testing, security testing, and user acceptance testing to ensure system stability, data consistency, and seamless integration.\\r\\n•\\tWork closely with the global CORE team to test customer solutions, ensuring optimal performance and stability.\\r\\n•\\tPerform SQL database querying and troubleshooting to identify and resolve production issues effectively.\\r\\n•\\tSuccessfully updated multiple site servers from MES 2014 to MES 2020, ensuring improved system performance, security, and compatibility across all locations.\\r\\n\\r\\n•\\tRespond to and manage incoming support tickets raised by customers or internal users related to server issues and diagnose server problems, investigate the root cause of incidents, and implement solutions to resolve issues promptly and escalate complex issues to higher-level support or specialized teams when necessary.\\r\\n•\\tResolved numerous P2 incidents for MES within SLA, preventing production stoppages and contributing to a 20% increase in production efficiency.\\r\\n•\\tConduct RCA meeting with teams involved in incident bridge call to document the root cause of the issue and create action plan towards the permanent fix to avoid future recurrence.\\r\\n•\\tCoordinating with the CAB team if any change request needs to be placed towards the permanent fix and monitor pre and post change request impact.\\r\\n•\\tCoordinating with the Knowledge Management team if any new KB request needs to be created or any changes needs to be made.\\r\\n•\\tWork collaboratively with other IT teams to address cross-functional issues and improve overall manufact