,'Karnataka'),('be580ddc-54ab-4945-9583-78f20d1d9a49','895c2926-0596-4115-a3e5-03a9d8fe042d','1ee4d080-3a60-4e83-ba83-d1de1e725d54','IT Project Manager','it-project-manager-93-93','About the Role:&lt;br /&gt;Join our global IoT client team as an IT Project Manager. You will oversee IT/software development projects, manage distributed teams, and ensure seamless communication with global clients. The role demands strong project management skills, attention to detail, and the ability to deliver enterprise-level solutions on time.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;br /&gt;- Lead and manage end-to-end IT/software projects ensuring timely delivery and quality.&lt;br /&gt;- Coordinate daily standups and cross-team tasks across time zones.&lt;br /&gt;- Manage JIRA (or similar tools) for project tracking and reporting.&lt;br /&gt;- Act as the primary liaison between internal teams and Fortune 500 clients.&lt;br /&gt;- Understand IT infrastructure, system architecture, and technical requirements.&lt;br /&gt;- Monitor milestones, delivery schedules, and operational support activities.&lt;br /&gt;- Provide clear project updates, escalate risks, and ensure effective communication.&lt;br /&gt;- Maintain compliance, documentation, and best practices.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications:&lt;br /&gt;- Minimum 3 years of experience in IT project management or related roles.&lt;br /&gt;- Strong understanding of SDLC and project management methodologies (Agile/Scrum).&lt;br /&gt;- Proficiency in JIRA, Trello, Asana, or MS Project.&lt;br /&gt;- Knowledge of IT systems, infrastructure, or IoT concepts (sensors, gateways, hardware).&lt;br /&gt;- Excellent communication skills&amp;mdash;fluent in English (Spanish is a plus).&lt;br /&gt;- Experience handling enterprise-level clients (preferably Fortune 500).&lt;br /&gt;- Highly organized, detail-oriented, and capable of managing multiple priorities.','Information Technology','Contract','Mid',NULL,NU