ect timelines, deliverables, and resources to ensure successful completion.&lt;br /&gt;- Work closely with clients to understand their manufacturing processes and provide tailored solutions.&lt;br /&gt;- Provide ongoing technical support and troubleshooting for MES systems.&lt;br /&gt;- Conduct training sessions for clients to ensure effective system use.','Information Technology','Contract','Mid',NULL,NULL,'₹',1,'India','PAN India',0,0,NULL,'PUBLISHED','2026-01-19 07:00:00',0,0,'2025-08-13 08:49:54.000000','2025-11-21 04:44:21.000000','INTERNAL',NULL,'[\"Client Consultations\", \"Mes Implementation\", \"Problem Solving\", \"Project Management\", \"Rockwell Software\", \"Technical Support\"]','[\"- Competitive salary and performance-based incentives&lt;br /&gt;- Health and life insurance coverage&lt;br /&gt;- Professional training and certification programs&lt;br /&gt;- Opportunities for career growth and advancement&lt;br /&gt;- Collaborative and innovative work environment&lt;br /&gt;- Work with global clients and projects\"]','No Preference',1,5,'PAN India'),('de4f5fd8-5a1f-41c3-bbf9-3b3676032084','895c2926-0596-4115-a3e5-03a9d8fe042d','1ee4d080-3a60-4e83-ba83-d1de1e725d54','Tulip Support Analyst','tulip-support-analyst-121-121','We are looking for an experienced Tulip Support Analyst with 7&amp;ndash;8 years of experience to provide high-level application and technical support for Tulip systems within a GxP-regulated environment. The candidate will be responsible for troubleshooting, incident resolution, system configuration, and ensuring compliance with pharma/life science standards.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;---&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;1. Provide high-level Tulip application support as required.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;2. Perform root cause analysis and problem resolution within scope.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;3. Configure and maintain Tulip application functionalities.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br 